## found
Tucked out of sight: a love letter Yamcha wrote to himself. That belongs to Yamcha, in the Grand Hall: confront yamcha there.
(Finding 1 of the 4 Jaco needs.)
You find fresh scorch marks, the wallpaper still smoking. (evidence #4)
You find a patch of air so still your ki sense slides off it. (evidence #3)
You find a fork with a smear of birthday frosting. (evidence #2)
Tucked out of sight: a love poem to Launch, signed with a little third eye. That belongs to Tien, in the Robot Workshop: confront tien there.
Tucked out of sight: a wanted poster of Launch, blonde. That belongs to Launch, in the Robot Workshop: confront launch there.
Scribbled on the back: "never trust a stand in".
You find a trail of light, quick footprints through spilled punch. (evidence #1)
You find an untouched slice of cake, the fork never lifted. (evidence #5)
You find a single dark hair caught on a splinter. (evidence #6)
## inspect
The damage tells its own story: no mark at all; whoever it was simply went out like a light. Either the Lights Out Capsule from the Study, or the Dream Ray from the Family Lounge. Both are missing.
The stand-in's last telemetry: its heart capsule stopped between eleven and midnight.
## portraits
Four portraits hang here, left to right:
  Mrs. Briefs, capsule 6
  Trunks, capsule 4
  Dr. Briefs, capsule 2
  Bulma, capsule 3
A brass plaque below: Right to left, as they hang.
The lab keypad takes the four numbers in that order, as one code: press 1234 style, in the Lab Vestibule.
## confront
Tien sees a love poem to Launch, signed with a little third eye and goes pale. "I was going to give it to her. One day."
"So that is where I really was:"
At midnight: "In the Grand Hall, with Mai and Gohan. Meditating. It was loud."
Launch sees a wanted poster of Launch, blonde and goes pale. "I sneezed, all right? I went to look at the poster."
"So that is where I really was:"
At nine: "In the Family Lounge, with Yamcha and Krillin. Oh my, I think that is right!"
Yamcha sees a love letter Yamcha wrote to himself and goes pale. "I was reading it to the mirror. It is a good letter."
"So that is where I really was:"
At midnight: "In the Family Lounge, with Krillin and Dende. I was not hiding. Much."
